y_diff_min', min(family_diffs))\nprint('family_diff_mean', round(sum(family_diffs) / len(family_diffs), 2))\nprint('family_diff_nonzero', sum(d > 0 for d in family_diffs), '/', len(family_diffs))\nprint('multicolor_min', min(multicolor_counts))\nprint('multicolor_mean', round(sum(multicolor_counts) / len(multicolor_counts), 2))\nprint('multicolor_ge2', sum(c >= 2 for c in multicolor_counts), '/', len(multicolor_counts))\nPY\" in /home/lixinyu/snap/new\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\nindex 07daa00449d88022797bcc79ed9d83fc5698dd62..ed7905be4ed892cf4c2c1d5ce759e9c45d13a61f\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\n@@ -19,59 +19,96 @@\n \n \n # Design analysis:\n-# - concrete behavior:\n-#   The original task used the frame only as a container, then used outside same-color sprites plus legends\n-#   to repaint every placeholder with one flat target color. This fusion keeps the same object inventory\n-#   but makes the frame color an active code with two simultaneous effects:\n-#     blue frame (1): rotate every matched sprite 90 degrees clockwise, then repaint it with vertical stripes\n-#                     alternating between the two legend colors.\n-#     green frame (3): keep the sprite orientation, then repaint it with a checkerboard alternating between\n-#                      the two legend colors.\n-#   The outside legend for source color s is now an opaque N x 3 rectangle:\n-#     column 0 = all s\n-#     column 1 = all pattern color a\n-#     column 2 = all pattern color b\n-#   Example trace for a 4x4 placeholder of color 2:\n-#     original: placeholder 2 -> outside color-2 sprite mask M -> legend 2->7 -> output is M filled with 7.\n-#     fused blue frame: placeholder 2 -> outside color-2 sprite mask M -> rotate to rot90(M, clockwise)\n-#     -> legend gives colors (8,4) -> fill rotated sprite with vertical 8/4 stripes clipped by the mask.\n-#     fused green frame: same sprite lookup, but no rotation; legend colors (8,4) are arranged as a checker.\n-#   The difference is therefore not just \"multicolor output\" and not just \"frame-coded transform\":\n-#   the frame color selects both the geometric transform and the spatial repaint pattern.\n-# - complexity calibration:\n-#   Only two frame-rule categories are used, because ARC examples usually give just 2-4 demonstrations.\n-#   A larger rule table would be underdetermined. The repaint families are also limited to two visible motifs\n-#   (vertical stripes vs checkerboard), so the distinction is obvious by eye.\n-# - implicit assumptions audit:\n-#   The original solver assumed legends were two-color overlap glyphs and that repainting wrote one scalar color.\n-#   Both assumptions break here, so the solver now:\n-#     1. finds multicolor opaque legend rectangles with size N x 3,\n-#     2. reads a source tag column plus a two-color palette,\n-#     3. synthesizes the final N x N tile from the frame color,\n-#     4. applies the frame-coded rotation before clipping the tile with the sprite mask.\n-#   Sprite extraction still assumes exactly one same-color N x N bbox per placeholder color outside the frame,\n-#   with any extra disconnected cells fully contained in that bbox; the generator preserves that.\n-# - placement legality and cleanliness:\n-#   Legends are opaque rectangles, sprites are monochrome-on-bg patches, and all outside patches are placed with\n-#   a reserve grid plus one-cell padding, so they never overlap or merge accidentally. Frame colors are excluded\n-#   from all other objects, preventing frame/sprite/legend ambiguity.\n-# - visual observability:\n-#   The blue rule is made visible by rejecting masks invariant under 90-degree rotation. Pattern visibility is\n-#   backed by rejecting masks whose occupied cells would only hit one stripe/parity bucket. Thus the generated\n-#   outputs cannot silently collapse back to a monochrome recolor or to an unobservable rotation.\n-# - generator-backed new assumptions:\n-#   Every placeholder color has exactly one legend palette, every legend uses two colors distinct from the source\n-#   color, placeholders remain square NxN so rotation preserves bbox size, and the chosen frame color is random\n-#   across samples so both frame-coded behaviors appear in the dataset.\n+# a) 具体化与行为追踪\n+#   原题流程是：\n+#     1. 框内实心占位块按颜色索引框外同色精灵。\n+#     2. 再读一个 source->target legend，把所有放入框内的精灵统一改成单色。\n+#   融合后改成：\n+#     1. 框外同色精灵仍然提供“形状”。\n+#     2. 每个 source 颜色在框外不再只有一个 legend，而是同时给出两种 multicolor legend：\n+#        - 条纹 legend\n+#        - 棋盘格 legend\n+#        二者都用同一个 source 标签列开头，右侧都是 N x N 的多色图案样本。\n+#     3. 框架颜色不再只是装饰，而是一个全局控制码：\n+#        - 蓝框(1): 精灵先顺时针旋转 90 度，再选“条纹 legend”进行重着色。\n+#        - 绿框(3): 精灵不旋转，改用“棋盘格 legend”进行重着色。\n+#   一个 4x4 的具体追踪例子：\n+#     - 原题：框内颜色 2 -> 取框外颜色 2 的精灵 M -> legend 说 2->7 -> 输出是单色 7 的 M。\n+#     - 融合蓝框：框内颜色 2 -> 取精灵 M -> 旋转成 rot90(M) -> 在颜色 2 的两个候选 legend 里，\n+#       选条纹 tile T_stripe -> 输出是被 rot90(M) 裁剪后的 T_stripe。\n+#     - 融合绿框：框内颜色 2 -> 取精灵 M -> 不旋转 -> 选棋盘格 tile T_checker -> 输出是被 M 裁剪后的 T_checker。\n+#   差异点不再是“纯重着色”或“纯框色控制”单独发生，而是框色同时决定几何变换和应读取哪类多色图案。\n+# b) 复杂度校准\n+#   只保留两个 frame-rule 档位，避免 ARC 训练样例过少时映射不可判定。\n+#   图案家族也只保留两类：vertical stripes 与 checkerboard；视觉差异稳定且不依赖颜色编号语义。\n+#   每个 source 同时出现两种候选 legend，防止规则退化成“只看唯一 legend 就够了”。\n+# c) 隐式假设审查\n+#   原 solver 的这些前提被打破了：\n+#     - legend 是两个颜色重叠得到的小双色 glyph。\n+#     - legend 只给一个目标色，写回时可以按像素直接填同一个标量。\n+#     - frame color 不参与真正决策。\n+#   新 solver 因此显式改成：\n+#     - 用 monochromatic=False 识别完整不透明 multicolor legend 矩形。\n+#     - 要求每个 source 对应两张 legend，且能按 tile 内容分类为条纹 / 棋盘格。\n+#     - 根据 frame color 先选 family，再选对应 legend tile，再裁剪到 sprite mask。\n+#   仍保留并由 generator 保证的前提：\n+#     - 每个 source 颜色在框外恰有一个同色 sprite bbox，尺寸与占位块一致。\n+#     - 占位块仍为方形 NxN，因此蓝框旋转后 bbox 不变。\n+# d) 放置合法性\n+#   generator 仍用 reserve 网格和 1-cell padding 放置外部对象，确保 sprite/legend/frame 互不重叠、不断开、不越界。\n+#   外部对象不复用任一 frame color，避免 frame/sprite/legend 解析歧义。\n+# e) 视觉可观察性\n+#   蓝框输出必须同时表现“旋转 + 条纹”；绿框必须表现“无旋转 + 棋盘格”。\n+#   为此 generator 拒绝：\n+#     - 对 90 度旋转不变的 sprite mask；\n+#     - 在蓝框规则下只会落到同一列奇偶类的 mask；\n+#     - 在绿框规则下只会落到同一棋盘奇偶类的 mask。\n+#   这样多色效果和 frame-coded 差异都能在少量样例中直接看到。\n+# f) 可视化整洁度\n+#   仍保持“一个框 + 框外模板与图例”的原布局，只是每个 source 多出一个候选 legend。\n+#   不在框内叠加额外标记；图案都在原 sprite bbox 内完成，因此输出区域仍然清晰。\n+# g) 变化的可推断性\n+#   颜色变化不靠隐式编号，而靠结构线索：\n+#     - 相同 source 的两个候选 legend 都可见；\n+#     - 框色稳定对应条纹或棋盘格；\n+#     - 同色占位块会重复出现，使同一 family 的图案在同一张图中多次重现。\n+# 9) main() 的新隐式假设与 generator 对应保证\n+#   - `_extract_legends` 假设 legend 是 N x (N+1) 的不透明矩形，首列全是 source 色。\n+#     generator 直接构造此矩形。\n+#   - `_classify_pattern_tile` 假设 tile 属于受限 family 集合。\n+#     generator 只产生 vertical/checker 两类 tile。\n+#   - 最终写回循环假设 frame 选择的 family 对每个 source 都存在。\n+#     generator 为每个 source 固定生成这两张 legend，solver 再按 frame color 选其中一张。\n \n \n FRAME_RULES = {\n-    1: {\"turns\": 1, \"pattern\": \"vertical\"},  # blue\n-    3: {\"turns\": 0, \"pattern\": \"checker\"},   # green\n+    1: {\"turns\": 1, \"family\": \"vertical\"},  # blue frame\n+    3: {\"turns\": 0, \"family\": \"checker\"},   # green frame\n }\n FRAME_COLORS = tuple(sorted(FRAME_RULES))\n+PATTERN_FAMILIES = tuple(sorted({str(rule[\"family\"]) for rule in FRAME_RULES.values()}))\n RESERVE_MARK = 10\n \n+# === CFG: tunables ===\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n+TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n+MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_FILL_MIN = 0.5\n+SPRITE_FILL_MAX = 0.9\n+MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n+MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n+MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n+FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK = 4\n+CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n+CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n+FRAME_POS_JITTER_PROB = 0.25\n+PATCH_PADDING = 1\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+MASK_RETRIES = 250\n+\n \n def _find_frame(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n     \"\"\"\n@@ -116,9 +153,9 @@\n     return int(FRAME_RULES[frame_col][\"turns\"])\n \n \n-def _frame_pattern(frame_col: int) -> str:\n+def _frame_family(frame_col: int) -> str:\n     assert frame_col in FRAME_RULES, f\"unsupported frame color {frame_col}\"\n-    return str(FRAME_RULES[frame_col][\"pattern\"])\n+    return str(FRAME_RULES[frame_col][\"family\"])\n \n \n def _apply_frame_rule(mask: np.ndarray, frame_col: int) -> np.ndarray:\n@@ -126,39 +163,61 @@\n     return np.rot90(mask, -turns).copy() if turns else mask.copy()\n \n \n-def _build_pattern_tile(shape: tuple[int, int], frame_col: int, color_a: int, color_b: int) -> np.ndarray:\n+def _build_pattern_tile(shape: tuple[int, int], family: str, color_a: int, color_b: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     h, w = map(int, shape)\n     rr, cc = np.indices((h, w))\n-    family = _frame_pattern(frame_col)\n     if family == \"vertical\":\n         selector = cc % 2\n     elif family == \"checker\":\n         selector = (rr + cc) % 2\n     else:\n-        raise AssertionError(f\"unknown pattern family {family}\")\n+        raise AssertionError(f\"unsupported family {family}\")\n     return np.where(selector == 0, int(color_a), int(color_b)).astype(int)\n \n \n-def _extract_legend_palettes(\n+def _classify_pattern_tile(tile: np.ndarray) -> str | None:\n+    if tile.ndim != 2 or min(tile.shape) < 2:\n+        return None\n+    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(tile)]\n+    if len(colors) != 2:\n+        return None\n+\n+    a = int(tile[0, 0])\n+    b = int(tile[0, 1])\n+    if a == b:\n+        return None\n+\n+    vertical = _build_pattern_tile(tile.shape, \"vertical\", a, b)\n+    if np.array_equal(tile, vertical):\n+        return \"vertical\"\n+\n+    checker = _build_pattern_tile(tile.shape, \"checker\", a, b)\n+    if np.array_equal(tile, checker):\n+        return \"checker\"\n+\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _extract_legends(\n     g: np.ndarray,\n     outside: np.ndarray,\n     bg: int,\n     frame_col: int,\n     placeholder_colors: set[int],\n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-) -> tuple[dict[int, tuple[int, int]], np.ndarray]:\n+) -> tuple[dict[int, dict[str, np.ndarray]], np.ndarray]:\n     masked = np.full_like(g, bg)\n     masked[outside] = g[outside]\n     comps = find_components(masked, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=False, return_format=\"dict\")\n \n-    palette_map: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n+    legend_tiles: dict[int, dict[str, np.ndarray]] = {}\n     legend_mask = np.zeros(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n \n     for comp in comps:\n         r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, comp[\"bbox\"])\n         h = _bbox_h((r0, c0, r1, c1))\n         w = _bbox_w((r0, c0, r1, c1))\n-        if w != 3:\n+        if w != h + 1:\n             continue\n \n         sub = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n@@ -175,44 +234,109 @@\n         if not np.all(sub[:, 0] == src_col):\n             continue\n \n-        color_a = int(sub[0, 1])\n-        color_b = int(sub[0, 2])\n-        if not np.all(sub[:, 1] == color_a):\n+        tile = sub[:, 1:]\n+        if tile.shape != phw[src_col]:\n             continue\n-        if not np.all(sub[:, 2] == color_b):\n+        if src_col in set(map(int, np.unique(tile))):\n             continue\n-        if len({src_col, color_a, color_b}) != 3:\n+\n+        family = _classify_pattern_tile(tile)\n+        if family is None:\n             continue\n \n-        assert src_col not in palette_map, f\"duplicate pattern legend for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-        palette_map[src_col] = (color_a, color_b)\n+        legend_tiles.setdefault(src_col, {})\n+        assert family not in legend_tiles[src_col], f\"duplicate {family} legend for source color {src_col}\"\n+        legend_tiles[src_col][family] = tile.copy()\n         legend_mask[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1] = True\n \n-    assert set(palette_map) == placeholder_colors, (\n-        f\"legend mappings {sorted(palette_map)} do not match placeholders {sorted(placeholder_colors)}\"\n+    assert set(legend_tiles) == placeholder_colors, (\n+        f\"legend sources {sorted(legend_tiles)} do not match placeholders {sorted(placeholder_colors)}\"\n     )\n-    return palette_map, legend_mask\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        got = set(legend_tiles[src_col])\n+        assert got == set(PATTERN_FAMILIES), f\"source color {src_col} has legend families {sorted(got)}\"\n+    return legend_tiles, legend_mask\n \n \n+def _extract_sprite_masks(\n+    g: np.ndarray,\n+    outside: np.ndarray,\n+    legend_mask: np.ndarray,\n+    bg: int,\n+    frame_col: int,\n+    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n+    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n+) -> dict[int, np.ndarray]:\n+    comps = []\n+    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) not in (bg, frame_col)]\n+    cid = 0\n+    for col in colors:\n+        for pts in components_mask((g == col) & outside, connectivity=4):\n+            pts_tuples = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]\n+            if all(bool(legend_mask[r, c]) for r, c in pts_tuples):\n+                continue\n+            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n+            comps.append(\n+                {\n+                    \"id\": cid,\n+                    \"col\": int(col),\n+                    \"pts\": pts_tuples,\n+                    \"bbox\": (r0, c0, r1, c1),\n+                }\n+            )\n+            cid += 1\n+\n+    sprite_masks: dict[int, np.ndarray] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no non-legend sprite found for color {src_col}\"\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n+        sized = [\n+            c\n+            for c in all_candidates\n+            if _bbox_h(c[\"bbox\"]) == want_h and _bbox_w(c[\"bbox\"]) == want_w\n+        ]\n+        assert len(sized) == 1, f\"expected one size-matched sprite for color {src_col}, found {len(sized)}\"\n+        base = sized[0]\n+        sr0, sc0, sr1, sc1 = base[\"bbox\"]\n+\n+        pts_set = set(base[\"pts\"])\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            if comp[\"id\"] == base[\"id\"]:\n+                continue\n+            r0, c0, r1, c1 = comp[\"bbox\"]\n+            assert sr0 <= r0 and sr1 >= r1 and sc0 <= c0 and sc1 >= c1, (\n+                f\"extra sprite component for color {src_col} is outside the base bbox\"\n+            )\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        mask = np.zeros((sr1 - sr0 + 1, sc1 - sc0 + 1), dtype=bool)\n+        for r, c in pts_set:\n+            mask[r - sr0, c - sc0] = True\n+        sprite_masks[src_col] = mask\n+\n+    return sprite_masks\n+\n+\n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Stamp frame-transformed sprites into a framed region, recoloring them with frame-coded multicolor patterns.\n+    Stamp frame-selected patterned sprites into a framed region using outside sprite templates and paired multicolor legends.\n \n     Input structure:\n     - bg background, one rectangular non-gray frame, and solid square placeholder blocks inside that frame.\n-    - Outside the frame: one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color, plus one opaque N x 3 legend\n-      whose first column is the placeholder color and whose other two columns provide the two colors used for repainting.\n+    - Outside the frame: one monochrome sprite template per placeholder color, plus two opaque N x (N+1) legends for each source color.\n+      Each legend starts with a uniform source-color column and its right N x N tile is either a striped or checkerboard pattern sample.\n \n     Rule:\n     - Find the frame and the placeholder blocks inside it.\n-    - Use placeholder color to pick the matching outside sprite and use the legend to read that source color's two repaint colors.\n-    - Apply the transform encoded by the frame color to the sprite shape, then synthesize the repaint tile from the frame color:\n-      blue frames use vertical stripes, green frames use a checkerboard.\n-    - Stamp the transformed sprite into every matching placeholder box, clipping the synthesized pattern tile by the sprite mask.\n+    - Use placeholder color to pick the matching outside sprite shape.\n+    - Read both candidate legends for that source color, then let the frame color decide which legend family applies:\n+      blue frames select the striped legend and rotate the sprite 90 degrees clockwise; green frames select the checker legend and keep the sprite orientation.\n+    - Stamp the transformed sprite into every matching placeholder box, clipping the chosen legend tile by the sprite mask.\n \n     Key insight:\n-    - The legend no longer contains the full final picture by itself. It only gives the two recolor values, while the frame color\n-      determines both the sprite orientation and the arrangement family of those colors, so both cues must be combined.\n+    - The multicolor legends alone are not enough, because each source color deliberately has more than one candidate pattern.\n+      The frame color is the control code that tells you which pattern family to use and whether the sprite shape should be rotated first.\n     \"\"\"\n     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n     bg = get_bg(g)\n@@ -245,115 +369,56 @@\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n-\n-    palette_map, legend_mask = _extract_legend_palettes(g, outside, bg, frame_col, placeholder_colors, phw)\n \n-    comps = []\n-    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) not in (bg, frame_col)]\n-    cid = 0\n-    for col in colors:\n-        for pts in components_mask((g == col) & outside, connectivity=4):\n-            pts_tuples = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]\n-            if all(bool(legend_mask[r, c]) for r, c in pts_tuples):\n-                continue\n-            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            comps.append(\n-                {\n-                    \"id\": cid,\n-                    \"col\": int(col),\n-                    \"pts\": pts_tuples,\n-                    \"bbox\": (r0, c0, r1, c1),\n-                }\n-            )\n-            cid += 1\n-\n-    sprite_masks: dict[int, np.ndarray] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no non-legend sprite found for color {src_col}\"\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        sized = [c for c in all_candidates if _bbox_h(c[\"bbox\"]) == want_h and _bbox_w(c[\"bbox\"]) == want_w]\n-        assert len(sized) == 1, f\"expected one size-matched sprite for color {src_col}, found {len(sized)}\"\n-        base = sized[0]\n-        sr0, sc0, sr1, sc1 = base[\"bbox\"]\n+    legend_tiles, legend_mask = _extract_legends(g, outside, bg, frame_col, placeholder_colors, phw)\n+    sprite_masks = _extract_sprite_masks(g, outside, legend_mask, bg, frame_col, placeholder_colors, phw)\n \n-        pts_set = set(base[\"pts\"])\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            if comp[\"id\"] == base[\"id\"]:\n-                continue\n-            r0, c0, r1, c1 = comp[\"bbox\"]\n-            assert sr0 <= r0 and sr1 >= r1 and sc0 <= c0 and sc1 >= c1, (\n-                f\"extra sprite component for color {src_col} is outside the base bbox\"\n-            )\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        base_mask = np.zeros((sr1 - sr0 + 1, sc1 - sc0 + 1), dtype=bool)\n-        for r, c in pts_set:\n-            base_mask[r - sr0, c - sc0] = True\n-        sprite_masks[src_col] = _apply_frame_rule(base_mask, frame_col)\n-\n     out = crop.copy()\n     out[1:-1, 1:-1] = bg\n \n+    family = _frame_family(frame_col)\n     for src_col, (pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1) in placeholders:\n-        assert src_col in sprite_masks and src_col in palette_map, (\n-            f\"placeholder color {src_col} missing sprite or pattern legend\"\n+        assert src_col in sprite_masks, f\"missing sprite for color {src_col}\"\n+        assert src_col in legend_tiles and family in legend_tiles[src_col], (\n+            f\"missing {family} legend for color {src_col}\"\n         )\n-        mask = sprite_masks[src_col]\n+\n+        mask = _apply_frame_rule(sprite_masks[src_col], frame_col)\n+        tile = legend_tiles[src_col][family]\n         sh, sw = mask.shape\n         assert (pr1 - pr0 + 1, pc1 - pc0 + 1) == (sh, sw), (\n             f\"placeholder size does not match transformed sprite for color {src_col}\"\n         )\n-        color_a, color_b = palette_map[src_col]\n-        tile = _build_pattern_tile((sh, sw), frame_col, color_a, color_b)\n-        patch = np.full((sh, sw), bg, dtype=int)\n-        patch[mask] = tile[mask]\n-        paste(out, patch, pr0, pc0, transparent=bg)\n+        assert tile.shape == (sh, sw), f\"legend tile shape does not match sprite for color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        for dr, dc in zip(*np.where(mask)):\n+            out[pr0 + dr, pc0 + dc] = int(tile[dr, dc])\n \n     return out\n \n \n-# --------------- generator (combo) ---------------\n+def _legend(src: int, tile: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n+    src_col = np.full((tile.shape[0], 1), int(src), dtype=int)\n+    return np.hstack([src_col, np.asarray(tile, dtype=int)])\n \n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n-GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n-GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n-TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n-MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_FILL_MIN = 0.5\n-SPRITE_FILL_MAX = 0.9\n-MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n-MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n-MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n-FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK = 4\n-CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n-CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n-FRAME_POS_JITTER_PROB = 0.25\n-PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 400\n-MASK_RETRIES = 250\n \n+def _sprite_mask_is_usable(mask: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n+    rotated = np.rot90(mask, -1)\n+    if np.array_equal(mask, rotated):\n+        return False\n \n-def _legend(src: int, color_a: int, color_b: int, n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build an N x 3 legend: source tag + two palette columns.\"\"\"\n-    return np.column_stack(\n-        [\n-            np.full(n, int(src), dtype=int),\n-            np.full(n, int(color_a), dtype=int),\n-            np.full(n, int(color_b), dtype=int),\n-        ]\n-    )\n+    rr, cc = np.where(mask)\n+    if len(rr) == 0 or len(set(((r + c) % 2) for r, c in zip(rr, cc))) < 2:\n+        return False\n \n+    rr2, cc2 = np.where(rotated)\n+    if len(rr2) == 0 or len(set(int(c % 2) for c in cc2)) < 2:\n+        return False\n \n-def _masked_pattern_uses_both_colors(mask: np.ndarray, frame_col: int) -> bool:\n-    transformed = _apply_frame_rule(mask, frame_col)\n-    tile = _build_pattern_tile(mask.shape, frame_col, 1, 2)\n-    return len(set(map(int, np.unique(tile[transformed])))) == 2\n+    return True\n \n \n-def _sprite_mask(n: int, frame_col: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Generate a random NxN binary mask with visible frame-coded effects.\"\"\"\n+def _sprite_mask(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     lo = max((n * n + 1) // 2, int(np.ceil(SPRITE_FILL_MIN * n * n)))\n     hi = min(int(np.floor(SPRITE_FILL_MAX * n * n)), n * n - 1)\n \n@@ -383,13 +448,10 @@\n             r, c = random.choice(frontier)\n             mask[r, c] = True\n \n-        if np.array_equal(mask, np.rot90(mask, -1)):\n-            continue\n-        if not _masked_pattern_uses_both_colors(mask, frame_col):\n-            continue\n-        return mask\n+        if _sprite_mask_is_usable(mask):\n+            return mask\n \n-    raise RuntimeError(f\"failed to generate visible {n}x{n} sprite mask\")\n+    raise RuntimeError(f\"failed to generate usable {n}x{n} sprite mask\")\n \n \n def _colored_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n@@ -398,11 +460,9 @@\n     return out\n \n \n-def _patterned_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, frame_col: int, color_a: int, color_b: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    transformed = _apply_frame_rule(mask, frame_col)\n-    tile = _build_pattern_tile(mask.shape, frame_col, color_a, color_b)\n+def _patterned_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, tile: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     out = np.full(mask.shape, bg, dtype=int)\n-    out[transformed] = tile[transformed]\n+    out[mask] = np.asarray(tile, dtype=int)[mask]\n     return out\n \n \n@@ -479,15 +539,17 @@\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n     src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    palette_pool = [c for c in usable if c not in src_cols]\n-    if len(palette_pool) < 2:\n-        return None\n+    masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n) for src in src_cols}\n \n-    masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, frame_col) for src in src_cols}\n-    legend_palettes: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n+    legend_tiles: dict[int, dict[str, np.ndarray]] = {}\n     for src in src_cols:\n-        color_a, color_b = random.sample(palette_pool, 2)\n-        legend_palettes[src] = (color_a, color_b)\n+        pool = [c for c in usable if c != src]\n+        if len(pool) < 2:\n+            return None\n+        color_a, color_b = random.sample(pool, 2)\n+        legend_tiles[src] = {\n+            family: _build_pattern_tile((n, n), family, color_a, color_b) for family in PATTERN_FAMILIES\n+        }\n \n     ch, cw = _content_extent(n, rows, cols)\n     min_fh = max(MIN_FRAME_H, ch + 4)\n@@ -500,25 +562,24 @@\n     left_margin = random.randint(1, x_margin - 1)\n \n     _, filled_slots = _choose_empty_slots(rows, cols, empty_count)\n-    cell_colors = {}\n+    cell_colors: dict[tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n     for slot, col in zip(filled_slots[:k], src_cols):\n         cell_colors[slot] = col\n     for slot in filled_slots[k:]:\n         cell_colors[slot] = random.choice(src_cols)\n-    if len(filled_slots) > k and all(sum(1 for val in cell_colors.values() if val == src) == 1 for src in src_cols):\n-        return None\n \n     input_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg, frame_col)\n     output_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg, frame_col)\n+    active_family = _frame_family(frame_col)\n     for (rr, cc), src in cell_colors.items():\n         r0 = 1 + top_margin + rr * (n + 1)\n         c0 = 1 + left_margin + cc * (n + 1)\n         paste(input_frame, np.full((n, n), src, dtype=int), r0, c0)\n-        color_a, color_b = legend_palettes[src]\n-        patterned = _patterned_sprite(masks[src], frame_col, color_a, color_b, bg)\n+        transformed = _apply_frame_rule(masks[src], frame_col)\n+        patterned = _patterned_sprite(transformed, legend_tiles[src][active_family], bg)\n         paste(output_frame, patterned, r0, c0, transparent=bg)\n \n-    ext_area = k * (n * n + 3 * n + 12)\n+    ext_area = k * (n * n + 2 * n * (n + 1) + 16)\n     possible_dims = [\n         (h, w)\n         for h in range(*CANVAS_H_RANGE)\n@@ -542,9 +603,9 @@\n \n     patches: list[tuple[np.ndarray, bool]] = []\n     for src in src_cols:\n-        color_a, color_b = legend_palettes[src]\n         patches.append((_colored_sprite(masks[src], src, bg), True))\n-        patches.append((_legend(src, color_a, color_b, n), False))\n+        for family in PATTERN_FAMILIES:\n+            patches.append((_legend(src, legend_tiles[src][family]), False))\n     random.shuffle(patches)\n     patches.sort(key=lambda item: item[0].size, reverse=True)\n     for patch, transparent in patches:\n\n succeeded in 4389ms:\nframe_counts {1: 53, 3: 47}\nfamily_diff_min 82\nfamily_diff_mean 113.36\nfamily_diff_nonzero 100 / 100\nmulticolor_min 3\nmulticolor_mean 4.18\nmulticolor_ge2 100 / 100\n\ncodex\n我在做退化检查：一是把同一输入的框色切换成另一种规则，看输出是否必然变化；二是统计输出内部是否稳定出现至少两种非背景颜色，确认不是退化回单色重着色。\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\nindex 07daa00449d88022797bcc79ed9d83fc5698dd62..ed7905be4ed892cf4c2c1d5ce759e9c45d13a61f\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py\n@@ -19,59 +19,96 @@\n \n \n # Design analysis:\n-# - concrete behavior:\n-#   The original task used the frame only as a container, then used outside same-color sprites plus legends\n-#   to repaint every placeholder with one flat target color. This fusion keeps the same object inventory\n-#   but makes the frame color an active code with two simultaneous effects:\n-#     blue frame (1): rotate every matched sprite 90 degrees clockwise, then repaint it with vertical stripes\n-#                     alternating between the two legend colors.\n-#     green frame (3): keep the sprite orientation, then repaint it with a checkerboard alternating between\n-#                      the two legend colors.\n-#   The outside legend for source color s is now an opaque N x 3 rectangle:\n-#     column 0 = all s\n-#     column 1 = all pattern color a\n-#     column 2 = all pattern color b\n-#   Example trace for a 4x4 placeholder of color 2:\n-#     original: placeholder 2 -> outside color-2 sprite mask M -> legend 2->7 -> output is M filled with 7.\n-#     fused blue frame: placeholder 2 -> outside color-2 sprite mask M -> rotate to rot90(M, clockwise)\n-#     -> legend gives colors (8,4) -> fill rotated sprite with vertical 8/4 stripes clipped by the mask.\n-#     fused green frame: same sprite lookup, but no rotation; legend colors (8,4) are arranged as a checker.\n-#   The difference is therefore not just \"multicolor output\" and not just \"frame-coded transform\":\n-#   the frame color selects both the geometric transform and the spatial repaint pattern.\n-# - complexity calibration:\n-#   Only two frame-rule categories are used, because ARC examples usually give just 2-4 demonstrations.\n-#   A larger rule table would be underdetermined. The repaint families are also limited to two visible motifs\n-#   (vertical stripes vs checkerboard), so the distinction is obvious by eye.\n-# - implicit assumptions audit:\n-#   The original solver assumed legends were two-color overlap glyphs and that repainting wrote one scalar color.\n-#   Both assumptions break here, so the solver now:\n-#     1. finds multicolor opaque legend rectangles with size N x 3,\n-#     2. reads a source tag column plus a two-color palette,\n-#     3. synthesizes the final N x N tile from the frame color,\n-#     4. applies the frame-coded rotation before clipping the tile with the sprite mask.\n-#   Sprite extraction still assumes exactly one same-color N x N bbox per placeholder color outside the frame,\n-#   with any extra disconnected cells fully contained in that bbox; the generator preserves that.\n-# - placement legality and cleanliness:\n-#   Legends are opaque rectangles, sprites are monochrome-on-bg patches, and all outside patches are placed with\n-#   a reserve grid plus one-cell padding, so they never overlap or merge accidentally. Frame colors are excluded\n-#   from all other objects, preventing frame/sprite/legend ambiguity.\n-# - visual observability:\n-#   The blue rule is made visible by rejecting masks invariant under 90-degree rotation. Pattern visibility is\n-#   backed by rejecting masks whose occupied cells would only hit one stripe/parity bucket. Thus the generated\n-#   outputs cannot silently collapse back to a monochrome recolor or to an unobservable rotation.\n-# - generator-backed new assumptions:\n-#   Every placeholder color has exactly one legend palette, every legend uses two colors distinct from the source\n-#   color, placeholders remain square NxN so rotation preserves bbox size, and the chosen frame color is random\n-#   across samples so both frame-coded behaviors appear in the dataset.\n+# a) 具体化与行为追踪\n+#   原题流程是：\n+#     1. 框内实心占位块按颜色索引框外同色精灵。\n+#     2. 再读一个 source->target legend，把所有放入框内的精灵统一改成单色。\n+#   融合后改成：\n+#     1. 框外同色精灵仍然提供“形状”。\n+#     2. 每个 source 颜色在框外不再只有一个 legend，而是同时给出两种 multicolor legend：\n+#        - 条纹 legend\n+#        - 棋盘格 legend\n+#        二者都用同一个 source 标签列开头，右侧都是 N x N 的多色图案样本。\n+#     3. 框架颜色不再只是装饰，而是一个全局控制码：\n+#        - 蓝框(1): 精灵先顺时针旋转 90 度，再选“条纹 legend”进行重着色。\n+#        - 绿框(3): 精灵不旋转，改用“棋盘格 legend”进行重着色。\n+#   一个 4x4 的具体追踪例子：\n+#     - 原题：框内颜色 2 -> 取框外颜色 2 的精灵 M -> legend 说 2->7 -> 输出是单色 7 的 M。\n+#     - 融合蓝框：框内颜色 2 -> 取精灵 M -> 旋转成 rot90(M) -> 在颜色 2 的两个候选 legend 里，\n+#       选条纹 tile T_stripe -> 输出是被 rot90(M) 裁剪后的 T_stripe。\n+#     - 融合绿框：框内颜色 2 -> 取精灵 M -> 不旋转 -> 选棋盘格 tile T_checker -> 输出是被 M 裁剪后的 T_checker。\n+#   差异点不再是“纯重着色”或“纯框色控制”单独发生，而是框色同时决定几何变换和应读取哪类多色图案。\n+# b) 复杂度校准\n+#   只保留两个 frame-rule 档位，避免 ARC 训练样例过少时映射不可判定。\n+#   图案家族也只保留两类：vertical stripes 与 checkerboard；视觉差异稳定且不依赖颜色编号语义。\n+#   每个 source 同时出现两种候选 legend，防止规则退化成“只看唯一 legend 就够了”。\n+# c) 隐式假设审查\n+#   原 solver 的这些前提被打破了：\n+#     - legend 是两个颜色重叠得到的小双色 glyph。\n+#     - legend 只给一个目标色，写回时可以按像素直接填同一个标量。\n+#     - frame color 不参与真正决策。\n+#   新 solver 因此显式改成：\n+#     - 用 monochromatic=False 识别完整不透明 multicolor legend 矩形。\n+#     - 要求每个 source 对应两张 legend，且能按 tile 内容分类为条纹 / 棋盘格。\n+#     - 根据 frame color 先选 family，再选对应 legend tile，再裁剪到 sprite mask。\n+#   仍保留并由 generator 保证的前提：\n+#     - 每个 source 颜色在框外恰有一个同色 sprite bbox，尺寸与占位块一致。\n+#     - 占位块仍为方形 NxN，因此蓝框旋转后 bbox 不变。\n+# d) 放置合法性\n+#   generator 仍用 reserve 网格和 1-cell padding 放置外部对象，确保 sprite/legend/frame 互不重叠、不断开、不越界。\n+#   外部对象不复用任一 frame color，避免 frame/sprite/legend 解析歧义。\n+# e) 视觉可观察性\n+#   蓝框输出必须同时表现“旋转 + 条纹”；绿框必须表现“无旋转 + 棋盘格”。\n+#   为此 generator 拒绝：\n+#     - 对 90 度旋转不变的 sprite mask；\n+#     - 在蓝框规则下只会落到同一列奇偶类的 mask；\n+#     - 在绿框规则下只会落到同一棋盘奇偶类的 mask。\n+#   这样多色效果和 frame-coded 差异都能在少量样例中直接看到。\n+# f) 可视化整洁度\n+#   仍保持“一个框 + 框外模板与图例”的原布局，只是每个 source 多出一个候选 legend。\n+#   不在框内叠加额外标记；图案都在原 sprite bbox 内完成，因此输出区域仍然清晰。\n+# g) 变化的可推断性\n+#   颜色变化不靠隐式编号，而靠结构线索：\n+#     - 相同 source 的两个候选 legend 都可见；\n+#     - 框色稳定对应条纹或棋盘格；\n+#     - 同色占位块会重复出现，使同一 family 的图案在同一张图中多次重现。\n+# 9) main() 的新隐式假设与 generator 对应保证\n+#   - `_extract_legends` 假设 legend 是 N x (N+1) 的不透明矩形，首列全是 source 色。\n+#     generator 直接构造此矩形。\n+#   - `_classify_pattern_tile` 假设 tile 属于受限 family 集合。\n+#     generator 只产生 vertical/checker 两类 tile。\n+#   - 最终写回循环假设 frame 选择的 family 对每个 source 都存在。\n+#     generator 为每个 source 固定生成这两张 legend，solver 再按 frame color 选其中一张。\n \n \n FRAME_RULES = {\n-    1: {\"turns\": 1, \"pattern\": \"vertical\"},  